(2. About Chichén Itzá) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 762.4900000000000091 Td
(Chichén Itzá is one of the most important archaeological sites in the Americas. Located on the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 744.8899999999999864 Td
(Yucatán Peninsula in present-day Mexico, it was a major Maya political, religious and commercial) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 727.2899999999999636 Td
(centre from roughly 600 to 1200 CE. Its architecture blends Maya and central Mexican styles,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 709.6900000000000546 Td
(reflecting its role as a cultural crossroads.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 686.0900000000000318 Td
(In 1988 the site was designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and in 2007 it was named one of the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 668.4900000000000091 Td
(New Seven Wonders of the World. El Castillo — the great step pyramid at its heart — is a) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.157 g
50. 650.8899999999999864 Td
(masterpiece of Maya astronomy and engineering.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 12.5 Tf
14.3749999999999982 TL
0.118 g
50. 629.2899999999999636 Td
(A short chronology) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 609.7899999999999636 Td
(• c. 600–900 CE — Chichén Itzá rises as a regional power; the earliest large constructions appear.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 589.9900000000000091 Td
(• c. 900–1200 CE — The city's golden age. El Castillo, the Great Ball Court, the Temple of the Warriors and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 573.1900000000000546 Td
(the Observatory take their present form.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 553.3899999999999864 Td
(• c. 1250 CE — Power shifts to Mayapán; Chichén Itzá declines and is gradually abandoned.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 533.5899999999999181 Td
(• 1526–1546 — Spanish expeditions pass through the ruined city.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 513.7899999999999636 Td
(• 1841–1843 — John Lloyd Stephens and Frederick Catherwood bring Chichén Itzá to world attention.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 493.9899999999999523 Td
(• 1904–1911 — Large-scale excavation begins; the Sacred Cenote is dredged.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.176 g
50. 474.1899999999999409 Td
(• 1988 — UNESCO World Heritage listing. 2007 — Named a New Wonder of the World.) Tj
